<group prefix="WebGpuSharp.FFI.">
    <comment location="InstanceHandle">
        <summary>
			Context for all other WebGPU objects.
			This is the first thing you create when using WebGPU. Its primary use is to create <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.AdapterHandle"/> and <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.SurfaceHandle"/>.
		</summary>
    </comment>
    <group prefix="InstanceHandle.">
        <comment location="CreateSurface">
            <summary>                
                Creates a new surface targeting a given window/canvas/surface/etc..
            </summary>
			<param name="descriptor">The descriptor to use for the surface</param>
        </comment>
		<comment location="HasWGSLLanguageFeature">
			<summary>
				check if a WGSL language extensions is supported by this instance.
			</summary>
			<param name="feature">The feature to check for</param>
			<returns> true if the feature is supported, false otherwise.</returns>
		</comment>
		<comment location="ProcessEvents">
			<summary>
				Processes asynchronous events on this `Instance`, calling any callbacks for asynchronous operations created with <see cref="WebGpuSharp.CallbackMode.AllowProcessEvents"/>.
			</summary>
		</comment>
		<comment location="RequestAdapter">
			<summary>Retrieves an Adapter which matches the given <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.RequestAdapterOptionsFFI"/>.</summary>
			<param name="options">The options to use for the adapter</param>
			<param name="callbackInfo">The callback to call when the adapter is ready</param>
		</comment>
		<comment location="WaitAny">
			<summary> Wait for at least one Future in `futures` to complete, and call callbacks of the respective completed asynchronous operations.</summary>
			<param name="futureCount">The number of futures to wait for</param>
			<param name="futures">The futures to wait for</param>
			<param name="timeoutNS">The timeout in nanoseconds</param>
		</comment>
		<comment location="GetWGSLLanguageFeatures">
			<summary>Returns set of supported WGSL language extensions supported by this instance.</summary>
			<param name="features"> A pointer to struct to fill with supported extension</param>
			<returns>The status of the operation</returns>
		</comment>
    </group>
</group>